      "answer": "All tests pass now.\n\n**Root cause:** In `internal/ledger/ledger.go:49`, the `Balance` method had an inverted filter condition:\n\n```go\n// Before (bug):\nif e.AccountID != accountID || e.Currency == \"\" {\n    b += e.AmountCents  // added entries that DON'T match the account\n}\n\n// After (fix):\nif e.AccountID == accountID {\n    b += e.AmountCents  // only adds entries for the requested account\n}\n```\n\nThe `!=` meant it summed entries for *every other account*, and the `|| e.Currency == \"\"` clause was spurious noise. The fix changes `!=` to `==` and removes the extraneous currency check, matching the intended SQL logic (`WHERE account_id = $1`).",
      "agent_patch": "diff --git a/internal/ledger/ledger.go b/internal/ledger/ledger.go\nindex 5f31c1d..690c3c5 100644\n--- a/internal/ledger/ledger.go\n+++ b/internal/ledger/ledger.go\n@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@ func (l *Ledger) Balance(accountID string) int64 {\n \tdefer l.mu.Unlock()\n \tvar b int64\n \tfor _, e := range l.entries {\n-\t\tif e.AccountID != accountID || e.Currency == \"\" {\n+\t\tif e.AccountID == accountID {\n \t\t\tb += e.AmountCents\n \t\t}\n \t}\n",
